# Build outputs — everything here is regenerated, nothing here is source.
#
#   dist/, dist-v2/    python3 build.py [v2]
#   worklog-*.apk      ./build_apk.sh [v2]
#   android/**/build   gradle assembleDebug
#
# 근무기록-WorkLog.html is NOT an output — build.py unpacks it as the shell.
# Do not add it here. See CLAUDE.md, "Traps".

dist/
dist-v2/
*.apk
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/

# build_apk.sh rm -rf's this and re-copies dist-v2/ into it on every run.
# The pwa/icon-*.png next to icon-source.png are NOT ignored: build.py copies
# those into dist/, so a plain `python3 build.py v2` needs them present.
android/app/src/main/assets/www/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Machine-local Claude Code permissions — absolute paths from this laptop,
# nothing the app needs.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── 서명 열쇠 · signing secrets — never commit these ──
# keystore.properties holds the passwords for the upload key; the .jks/.keystore
# IS the upload key. Losing the key means never being able to update the app the
# workers already have; leaking it means someone else can sign as you. Neither
# belongs in a repository. The .example file next to it is the template and is
# tracked on purpose.
android/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
!android/keystore.properties.example

# Release outputs — regenerated by ./build_apk.sh release | bundle
*.aab
